Z||000009||fastback87||10-23-2001||05:27 PM||||Mine was doing the same thing awhile ago, It was my oil pressure sending unit and fuel pump.  The sending unit was causing the fuel pump to stay on with the ignition off or on.  I was hearing a whining noise and depending on how low the fuel was it started to sound a little sparky.  This would run down a new battery in about 2 days.  this might not be the same noise you are hearing but my fiero was running the battery down for about a year b4 I realized what the problem was.  the fix was about $30||||reg||1
